.SH NAME
section_divider \- See the module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
SectionDivider::new(title: impl Into<String>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBSectionDivider\fR: a section's name, a thin line running from it to the far end, and the section's action there. By default the action is the \fBtoggle\fR: a chevron that folds and unfolds the section, and pressing the name or the line does the same. Use it above a list the user can collapse (a queue's history, a long group).
.PP
.nf
.RS
SectionDivider::new("History").detail("12 tracks").open(open).on_toggle(Msg::ToggleHistory)
.RE
.fi
.PP
It draws the header only; the app owns \fBopen\fR and decides what to show under it (wrap the body in a \fBCollapsible\fR to animate it).
